at a\nunique split with vanishing coefficient valuation, then $\\delta(n) = 0$.\n\n\\section{Conjectures and future directions}\n\nThe bridge is a lax monoidal functor from $(\\NN \\to K, +, \\cc)$ to the min-plus\nsemiring of valuation profiles. The following target the lax/strict gap.\n\n\\begin{conjecture}[Transversality $\\Rightarrow$ equality]\n$\\tc(\\vp a, \\vp b)(n) = \\vp(a\\cc b)(n)$ holds whenever the antidiagonal infimum\n$\\inf_{i+j=n}(v(a_i)+v(b_j))$ is attained at a unique pair $(i,j)$ with vanishing\ncoefficient valuation (in the $p$-adic binomial model, $p \\nmid \\binom{n}{i}$).\n\\end{conjecture}\n\n\\begin{conjecture}[Newton polygons add]\nDefine the Newton profile $N(a)$ as the lower convex hull of $n \\mapsto v(a_n)$.\nThen $N(a \\cc b)$ equals the inf-convolution of $N(a)$ and $N(b)$ (Minkowski sum\nof polygons), with equality, upgrading the lax functor to a strict one after\npassing to convex hulls.\n\\end{conjecture}\n\n\\begin{conjecture}[Tropical differential calculus]\nThe shift $(\\mathrm{shift}\\,a)(n) = a(n+1)$ satisfies\n$\\vp(\\mathrm{shift}\\,a)(n) = \\vp(a)(n+1)$ exactly, and pointing\n$(\\mathrm{point}\\,a)(n) = n\\cdot a(n)$ satisfies\n$\\vp(\\mathrm{point}\\,a)(n) \\ge \\vp(a)(n)$ with equality iff $v(n) = 0$.\n\\end{conjecture}\n\n\\begin{conjecture}[Tropical composition]\nSpecies substitution $(F \\circ G)$ admits a tropical analogue: $\\vp(\\mathrm{subst}\\,a\\,b)$\nis bounded below by a min-plus composition infimum over set partitions, governed\nin the $p$-adic case by valuations of multinomial coefficients (a multivariate\nKummer phenomenon).\n\\end{conjecture}\n\n\\section{Conclusion}\n\nWe have built a clean bridge from the multiplicative world of generating-function\nconvolution to the additive, order-theoretic world of tropical valuation profiles\nand proved it sound: the min-plus convolution of valuation profiles never exceeds\nthe valuation profile of the Cauchy convolution. The result holds in maximal\nalgebraic gene